 some money and for guns and  schools which of course be an absolute  disaster funding for deal  with opioid addiction that's a good  thing 10% increase to veteran health  care which is of course fine but we have  to consider the total funding for all  types of health care and we can't fully  do that until we talk about what is  being cut education voucher program  which is once again a handout to those  who are looking to [ __ ] public  education and to provide money to  charter schools and private schools etc  a total disaster and 200 billion dollars  for infrastructure as we know  infrastructure spending in general is  stimulative it's necessary  we have aging infrastructure in the  United States but the way that Donald  Trump wants to do infrastructure  spending is a crony capitalist handout  to his friends and the way things have  been going probably relatives as well so  these are the notable Trump budget  increases let's look now at the other  side of the ledger which is what is  being cut either partially or fully in  Donald Trump's proposed 4.75 trillion  dollar budget that we saw yesterday  starting with one point nine trillion in  cuts to various safety net programs  which includes cuts in funding for both  Medicaid and Medicare there it is I told  you a year ago they blew up the budget  and they would later say the they blew  up the deficit rather the deficits so  big that we now need to start cutting  Medicaid and Medicare that is exactly  what the Trump administration is  proposing but not just that  also a twenty six billion dollar cut to  the social security disability program  the Trump budget wants to save three  hundred and twenty seven billion dollars  by adding some new work requirements for  adult food stamp and housing recipients  they believe that will kick off a bunch  of people from those programs saving  them three hundred and twenty seven  billion Donald Trump wants to cut  funding for the Environmental Protection  Agency by thirty one percent last thing  we should be doing right now as we more  and more rapidly destroy our planet a  500 million dollar  hut-2 NASA which I disagree with  ideologically but also even if you're a  sort of national security conservative  you should want to fund NASA because so  much of what NASA does so much of space  exploration and research for better or  worse leads to technologies and  developments that are useful for  national security 70 percent cut to  renewable energy research exactly  opposite what our priorities should be  eliminates climate change programs at  multiple agencies so different agencies  within them have elements of climate  change related research Trump  specifically is eliminating funding for  those programs within many of these  agencies this includes a 14 percent cut  to the Interior Department this includes  a 10 percent cut to the Education  Department and then there are a bunch of  little cuts you could call it death by a  thousand paper cuts to programs like low  income after-school programs public  service loan forgiveness subsidized  Stafford loans and work-study absolute  disaster  another interesting thing I guess is  maybe a word for it is that Trump is  proposing a way to cut spending on  prescription drugs which President Obama  already tried and actually failed with  so it's almost like taking a part of  Obama's health care reform that didn't  work and just trying to breathe life  back into it sort of like he's tried to  do with the coal industry now you might  recall that Donald Trump promised to pay  off the national debt within eight years  if given eight years as president this  budget if it were approved would not  balance for 15 years guaranteed we would  maintain massive deficits for 15 years  we can debate whether deficits are a  good bad medium or it depends but the  promise was that he would pay off the  debt in eight years instead he's doing  the opposite by virtue of these  proposals and tax policy and trade  policy and increasing that deficit he  claims that free collar  and healthcare for all are just too  expensive but those things make sense  and instead we're adding 5% to the  military budget not only unnecessary but  immoral and a complete misuse of  resources now I I'm getting to the thing  a lot of people are waiting for me to  say which is Congress actually  determines spending right Congress will  ultimately determine spending levels  this is what Trump is asking for  presidents never get exactly what they  asked for in White House budgets this is  a starting point ultimately it's going  to be up to the House and Senate to  decide how we are going to be spending  taxpayer money Democrats in both the  House and Senate already say that this  budget is dead on arrival you might  recall that even when Republicans  controlled both the House and Senate for  the first part of Donald Trump's  presidency Trump's budgets were not  passed as submitted with Democrats now  controlling the house this obviously is  not going to pass as submitted it's a  political document I don't even think  Republicans would dream of Medicare cuts  as we're ramping up to the 2020 election  I am sure that they value  self-preservation enough to realize  that's a bad idea  but as proposed let's take it at face  value as in this is what Trump proposed  because this is what he wants it's  flagrantly irresponsible and also  completely destructive if it were to  become a reality
 

